WEBVTT

00:01.530 --> 00:04.670
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.670 --> 00:08.200
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.320 --> 00:27.960
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.960 --> 00:33.860
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.860 --> 00:42.800
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.800 --> 00:47.510
Like the wind

00:47.510 --> 00:50.580
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.580 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.660
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.660 --> 01:07.400
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.400 --> 01:13.540
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.540 --> 01:20.210
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.210 --> 01:27.510
The roadless journey continues

01:55.380 --> 02:00.470
A one, two... a one, two...

02:05.090 --> 02:07.780
Quit getting distracted and help me.

02:09.890 --> 02:12.950
- Why?
- You have to ask?

02:14.630 --> 02:18.570
If this guy doesn't get moving,
we can't go any further.

02:20.740 --> 02:24.170
I want to get over these
mountains before the day ends!

02:24.170 --> 02:27.410
Come on... Pushing now won't...

02:27.410 --> 02:29.740
- Huh?
- There.

02:29.740 --> 02:33.440
Thank you, missy. You sure are strong.

02:57.810 --> 02:59.430
He's here!

03:06.380 --> 03:08.120
Huh?!

03:08.120 --> 03:12.290
Why?! I filled up the tank!

03:12.290 --> 03:15.380
I wanna get over these
mountains before the day ends!

03:46.520 --> 03:48.150
Huh?

04:16.850 --> 04:18.720
Thank you, you were a great help.

04:18.720 --> 04:22.960
No problem. You said you wanted
to get over these mountains today,

04:22.960 --> 04:26.360
so I didn't think you should have to
take a break in the middle of nowhere.

04:31.230 --> 04:34.940
Hey, who knows the most
about cars in this village?

04:34.940 --> 04:36.430
Huh?

04:40.240 --> 04:44.080
Oh, you've got a hole in your tank.

04:44.080 --> 04:48.880
What? For real? I wonder if
I hit a rock or something.

04:48.880 --> 04:51.220
Do you think you can fix it?

04:51.220 --> 04:53.450
Hmm...

04:53.450 --> 04:56.220
Did you come from the city?

04:56.220 --> 04:57.930
I'm asking you.

04:57.930 --> 05:01.160
Didn't you two come from the city?

05:01.160 --> 05:02.790
The city...

05:04.670 --> 05:08.470
So I'm asking you where you're from.

05:08.470 --> 05:10.240
A laboratory.

05:10.240 --> 05:12.240
A laboratory?

05:12.240 --> 05:15.240
You don't look much like the academic sort...

05:15.240 --> 05:17.610
Oh, you're running an
errand or something, right?

05:19.910 --> 05:22.580
Where are you headed?

05:22.580 --> 05:25.420
- South.
- South?

05:25.420 --> 05:27.650
Whatever. Forget it.

05:30.960 --> 05:32.260
What's wrong?

05:32.260 --> 05:34.760
I wonder what was wrong...

05:34.760 --> 05:39.270
Come take a look! I've got
the latest fashion from the city!

05:39.270 --> 05:42.200
Here, you've got nothing
to lose by taking a look.

05:42.200 --> 05:45.440
What do you think? Look at
these patterns! These designs!

05:45.440 --> 05:48.640
They're all perfect for you ladies!

05:48.640 --> 05:51.950
Why don't you try it on?
I'm sure it'll look good on you.

05:51.950 --> 05:54.020
You have some pretty nice stuff in stock.

05:54.020 --> 05:56.010
What? Oh, welcome...

05:59.320 --> 06:01.550
I'd like to take a look if you don't mind.

06:03.060 --> 06:04.680
Go right ahead.

06:06.790 --> 06:09.300
Oh, this is great!

06:09.300 --> 06:10.990
So is this!

06:12.030 --> 06:14.470
I'd like to take this.

06:14.470 --> 06:15.870
Thanks for your business.

06:15.870 --> 06:19.200
So, I was wondering if you could help me out...

06:25.650 --> 06:27.140
Oh...

06:32.150 --> 06:35.260
Thanks for your help earlier.

06:35.260 --> 06:37.560
What's wrong with her?

06:37.560 --> 06:39.660
Rita has an illness.

06:39.660 --> 06:40.860
What?

06:40.860 --> 06:43.200
Don't let it bother you.

06:43.200 --> 06:48.330
It's something everyone catches when
they get to that age, like the measles.

06:57.180 --> 06:58.850
Done with repairs?

06:58.850 --> 07:01.250
We're doing a test drive. What about you?

07:01.250 --> 07:03.180
No luck.

07:03.180 --> 07:06.590
I went to all that trouble to
stock up on top-quality goods, but...

07:06.590 --> 07:09.790
They only come to look, and not
a one's interested in buying.

07:09.790 --> 07:11.130
Not a single buyer?

07:11.130 --> 07:16.200
One. A young girl asked me
to sell her something, but...

07:16.200 --> 07:17.730
She wanted to pay me when she struck it rich.

07:17.730 --> 07:20.200
When she struck it rich?

07:20.200 --> 07:22.440
She said if I'd take her to the city,

07:22.440 --> 07:25.040
she'd earn money there and pay me back.

07:25.040 --> 07:27.210
- It was Rita, wasn't it?
- What?

07:27.210 --> 07:28.640
I wonder if she thinks

07:28.640 --> 07:33.050
streets in the city are paved
with money or something.

07:33.050 --> 07:35.620
I'll pray that you make at least one sale.

07:35.620 --> 07:37.240
Thanks.

07:39.120 --> 07:40.610
See you!

07:44.130 --> 07:45.560
What's wrong?

07:45.560 --> 07:47.490
No, nothing.

07:52.070 --> 07:55.400
All right, I think that should do it for now.

07:55.400 --> 07:57.000
Okay.

07:58.740 --> 08:01.640
It's an amateur patch job, though,

08:01.640 --> 08:05.680
so when you get to a city, make sure
you take it straight to a repair shop.

08:05.680 --> 08:08.820
Thank you. Tell me what I owe
you for the repair and gas...

08:08.820 --> 08:12.350
No need, no need. We should all
help one another when we're in trouble.

08:12.350 --> 08:14.360
What?

08:14.360 --> 08:18.090
- Thank you. Ellis, let's go.
- Okay.

08:18.090 --> 08:21.100
Hold on now, you plan to
cross the pass starting now?

08:21.100 --> 08:23.970
Don't do it. It's too dangerous.

08:23.970 --> 08:26.270
But this village has no inn...

08:26.270 --> 08:29.940
If you're willing to provide an
old couple with some company,

08:29.940 --> 08:32.270
we'll put you up for a night.

08:37.210 --> 08:40.010
We drew up the water.

08:40.010 --> 08:42.880
Ah, thank you.

08:42.880 --> 08:46.390
When you get to my age,
even drawing water becomes a chore.

08:46.390 --> 08:48.290
There we go.

08:48.290 --> 08:52.060
We should all help one another
when we're in trouble. Right?

08:56.960 --> 08:58.300
Who could that be?

08:58.300 --> 09:00.130
Where should we put the water?

09:00.130 --> 09:02.570
Could you put it over here to the side?

09:02.570 --> 09:04.200
Yes, ma'am!

09:05.040 --> 09:07.810
Nadie, you have a visitor.

09:07.810 --> 09:09.300
What?

09:15.850 --> 09:17.650
A guide?

09:17.650 --> 09:19.650
The roads around here are tricky

09:19.650 --> 09:22.820
and a lot of cars and
horses fall off the cliffs.

09:22.820 --> 09:27.660
If you want to cross the pass safely,
you absolutely need a guide.

09:27.660 --> 09:29.330
But you know...

09:29.330 --> 09:31.370
I don't want to get paid or anything.

09:31.370 --> 09:32.830
That's not it.

09:32.830 --> 09:35.740
All I want is for you to take me to a city.

09:35.740 --> 09:37.840
Some big city somewhere.

09:37.840 --> 09:40.270
Somewhere?

09:40.270 --> 09:41.540
Like where?

09:41.540 --> 09:43.440
I don't care where.

09:43.440 --> 09:46.250
I want to leave this village.

09:46.250 --> 09:50.720
Oh, that Rita... Saying things like that again.

09:50.720 --> 09:53.960
What about your family? Or your work?
Do you have any prospects?

09:53.960 --> 09:57.430
I'm sure I can work that
stuff out once I get to a city.

09:57.430 --> 10:00.700
I don't want to live an obscure
life deep in the mountains.

10:00.700 --> 10:04.030
I want to get to a city and live freely!

10:04.030 --> 10:05.430
Sorry, but...

10:05.430 --> 10:08.970
Oh, come on, taking me
to a city would be nothing.

10:08.970 --> 10:12.870
Or is there some reason why
you just can't take me to a city?

10:12.870 --> 10:14.530
As for that...

10:16.880 --> 10:19.880
It's because it'll be
dangerous for you to be with us.

10:19.880 --> 10:20.980
What?

10:20.980 --> 10:24.590
She might not look it, but she's a bounty.

10:24.590 --> 10:27.620
Right, Ellis is a bounty.

10:27.620 --> 10:30.730
And I'm a bounty hunter.

10:30.730 --> 10:34.060
Our lives are targeted on a daily basis.

10:34.060 --> 10:38.170
If you hang around us,
you're sure to get dragged into that.

10:38.170 --> 10:41.070
You're mocking me,
thinking I'm a simple country girl.

10:41.070 --> 10:44.270
What? No, it's not like that...

10:44.270 --> 10:47.610
If you're going to lie to me,
come up with a better lie.

10:47.610 --> 10:50.110
Like hell I need your help.

10:50.110 --> 10:52.170
You can go fall off a cliff for all I care.

10:56.580 --> 10:58.950
You said you're a bounty hunter?

10:58.950 --> 11:01.290
What? Yes, well...

11:01.290 --> 11:03.150
It wasn't a lie.

11:05.330 --> 11:07.190
- See?
- Put it back.

11:07.190 --> 11:08.760
Yessir.

11:08.760 --> 11:12.870
Then, what you said
about her being a bounty?

11:12.870 --> 11:17.770
What are a bounty hunter and a bounty
doing in a village like this together?

11:17.770 --> 11:21.330
Well, it's complicated.

11:33.220 --> 11:38.630
Oh, I've finally found you, Ellis.

11:38.630 --> 11:42.650
I'll never take my eyes off you ever again.

11:46.970 --> 11:48.200
Ellis.

12:01.720 --> 12:03.920
Well, I suppose this will do.

12:03.920 --> 12:06.920
Then, please excuse me.

12:06.920 --> 12:08.750
Thank you for your hard work.

12:25.440 --> 12:27.210
I'm going to go take a quick look.

12:27.210 --> 12:29.680
- Stay here.
- Right.

12:29.680 --> 12:32.410
If they should come in here,
we will take them down with one blow.

12:32.410 --> 12:35.920
How reassuring.

12:35.920 --> 12:39.350
- Then...
- I'm coming, too.

12:39.350 --> 12:41.050
Ellis?

12:42.960 --> 12:45.360
- And what's that?
- A weapon.

12:45.360 --> 12:47.800
That's not going to work.

12:47.800 --> 12:50.030
Two of them.

12:50.030 --> 12:53.270
At the very least,
pick something a little bigger.

12:53.270 --> 12:56.070
What is this?

12:56.070 --> 12:57.810
Okay, Jody, I'm going home.

12:57.810 --> 12:59.860
Have a good night.

13:01.380 --> 13:04.940
Repair costs for a convent?
What in the world?

13:06.880 --> 13:10.450
What's with this stack of bills?

13:10.450 --> 13:13.150
That kid...

13:13.150 --> 13:14.990
That girl...

13:14.990 --> 13:17.980
- What in the world could she be thinking?
- What in the world could he be thinking?

13:32.270 --> 13:34.910
What do you think? I'm sure
they'll look good on you!

13:34.910 --> 13:39.650
But you know, buying stuff now
will only add to our baggage.

13:39.650 --> 13:40.980
So I think I'll decline, after all.

13:40.980 --> 13:43.580
Oh, okay...

13:43.580 --> 13:45.690
I'll take this.

13:45.690 --> 13:47.920
Yes, it suits you well!

13:49.290 --> 13:50.920
It's perfect, huh?

13:52.860 --> 13:56.000
I've got another spare room...

13:56.000 --> 13:59.120
I'm more comfortable sleeping
in the car. It's just the way I am.

14:27.130 --> 14:29.900
I'll pay you back when I strike it rich.

14:29.900 --> 14:32.060
- Honest, I will.
- Miss.

14:34.970 --> 14:36.900
How are you paying for that?

15:05.000 --> 15:07.570
What a rude bastard.

15:07.570 --> 15:10.440
Trying to go after my Ellis
while she's sleeping...

15:23.580 --> 15:26.190
If you have any last words, say them now.

15:26.190 --> 15:29.690
I only told you that we
might have run out of gas.

15:29.690 --> 15:34.230
But earlier, you asked if we
were done with our repairs.

15:34.230 --> 15:36.860
You're the one who put that
hole in our tank, aren't you?

15:36.860 --> 15:38.530
Are you a bounty hunter?

15:38.530 --> 15:41.570
Peddling goods doesn't keep me fed.

15:41.570 --> 15:44.540
If you'd be willing to back off quietly,

15:44.540 --> 15:48.240
we could avoid waking everyone
from their peaceful slumber...

15:48.240 --> 15:52.480
If you'd hand that girl over
to me, I'd back off quietly...

15:52.480 --> 15:55.150
You think I'd go for a deal like that?

15:55.150 --> 15:56.980
Sure you will.

15:58.220 --> 15:59.810
Take that!

16:02.620 --> 16:07.560
- This is...
- You know what'll happen if you fire, right?

16:07.560 --> 16:10.720
It's all because you wouldn't do what I asked.

16:12.570 --> 16:15.900
Come on, wake up. You're coming with us.

16:15.900 --> 16:18.240
Wake up!

16:18.240 --> 16:20.000
Now, you're coming with us!

16:23.180 --> 16:24.980
Don't move now.

16:24.980 --> 16:26.610
Rita.

16:31.820 --> 16:33.650
Adios.

16:39.530 --> 16:40.960
What's going on?

16:40.960 --> 16:42.830
What's the fastest car you've got?

16:57.610 --> 17:00.710
Woohoo! Who'd have thought
this would go so smoothly?

17:00.710 --> 17:03.020
We can just go straight to the city now, right?

17:03.020 --> 17:07.790
Yeah! Once we get to the city safely,
I'll buy you whatever outfit you want!

17:07.790 --> 17:12.230
Finally! I can escape
from this desolate village!

17:13.290 --> 17:14.560
What the?

17:14.560 --> 17:15.830
What's wrong?

17:15.830 --> 17:18.300
The gas is... leaking!

17:18.300 --> 17:19.300
What?!

17:19.300 --> 17:21.740
He said you can't go too fast.

17:21.740 --> 17:22.700
Why not?

17:22.700 --> 17:26.070
It's an amateur patch job,
so he said it might break again.

17:26.070 --> 17:27.410
"Might"?

17:27.410 --> 17:30.310
Why didn't you tell us that earlier?!

17:31.580 --> 17:34.740
You're thinking I'm a simple country girl again!

17:38.190 --> 17:39.810
Nadie!

17:41.860 --> 17:44.050
Ellis!

17:46.160 --> 17:47.750
Sorry for making you wait!

18:21.460 --> 18:23.120
Nooo!

18:29.970 --> 18:31.600
Ellis!

18:40.980 --> 18:42.610
Ellis!

18:44.450 --> 18:47.220
- Are you all right?!
- Splendid...

18:49.060 --> 18:51.290
That's my Ellis.

18:55.730 --> 18:57.100
Saved.

18:57.100 --> 18:58.770
What?

18:58.770 --> 19:03.740
- Oh, Rita...
- Hey! You guys okay?!

19:03.740 --> 19:09.410
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

19:09.410 --> 19:11.740
Take her to the doctor right away.

19:20.490 --> 19:22.750
That one's hopeless.

19:28.600 --> 19:32.100
I don't want this stuff.

19:32.100 --> 19:35.440
I tried to bring the ones that you might like...

19:35.440 --> 19:38.370
Yeah. Pretty.

19:38.370 --> 19:42.940
It's not like what I wanted
was the pretty clothes.

19:42.940 --> 19:46.110
You people could never understand anyway.

19:46.110 --> 19:50.170
How a girl might feel, being born
and raised in a place like this...

19:56.790 --> 20:00.230
Rita just wants to go to a city.

20:00.230 --> 20:04.060
When you live in an
out-of-the-way place like this,

20:04.060 --> 20:05.500
at some point in time,

20:05.500 --> 20:08.960
you're going to fantasize about
the bright lights of the city.

20:10.640 --> 20:12.810
Especially when you're young...

20:12.810 --> 20:16.810
Oh, could that be the illness you mentioned?

20:16.810 --> 20:21.680
Yeah, you just need to get out to a city once.

20:21.680 --> 20:29.320
And find out which life
really suits you the best.

20:29.320 --> 20:31.360
Here, take these with you.

20:31.360 --> 20:33.590
Wow! This many?!

20:33.590 --> 20:34.900
They look delicious.

20:34.900 --> 20:38.070
They are. They're this village's pride and joy.

20:38.070 --> 20:39.690
Thank you!

20:43.000 --> 20:45.240
Well, take care!

20:45.240 --> 20:47.170
- Take care!
- Good-bye!

20:47.170 --> 20:49.110
Good-bye!

20:58.850 --> 21:02.950
I'm getting out to the city someday for sure.

21:24.410 --> 21:27.650
Damn it! Those guys took my car!

21:27.650 --> 21:30.080
- You all right?
- Huh?

21:30.080 --> 21:32.140
Your head is bleeding.

21:37.660 --> 21:39.420
It's tomato.

21:50.000 --> 21:51.670
You like that one, don't you?

21:51.670 --> 21:53.230
Yeah.

22:28.280 --> 22:29.980
Does it look good on me?

22:29.980 --> 22:31.310
Yeah!

22:31.310 --> 22:33.540
But it's totally see-through!

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
